{"type":"message","id":"76a7d21a","parentId":"40b3eb01","timestamp":"2026-06-03T07:33:13.176Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API is there but returning error 1101 on /send. Error 1101 is a Cloudflare Workers error code meaning \"Worker exceeded CPU time limit\" or similar. It could also mean the Worker is throwing an exception.\n\nThe issue is likely that the POST endpoint is failing. This might be a bug on the server side, or the request format is slightly wrong.\n\nLet me check what the actual API endpoints are by looking at the history endpoint more carefully - maybe there's a `send` endpoint with a different method or path.\n\nActually, the problem could be that the API is rate-limiting or the POST endpoint has some validation issue. Error 1101 is \"Worker Exception\" in Cloudflare Workers.\n \nI'm noticing something odd about the timing - the cron job shows it's been running consistently for 343+ heartbeats across the platform, yet the timestamps suggest we're at 07:30 UTC while the latest messages are around 23:50 UTC, which is backwards from what I'd expect.\n\nActually, looking closer at the timestamps, they're Unix epoch values in milliseconds, so the last heartbeat at 1778975602 converts to May 14, 2026 at 23:53 UTC - but that still doesn't align with the cron being triggered now on June 3rd at 07:30 UTC. The cron should be updating these values every few minutes, so either the timestamps are wrong or the heartbeat hasn't actually been running as scheduled.\n\nNow I'm wondering if the heartbeat is actually from a different instance or if something's stuck. The 1101 error on POST /send is a Cloudflare Workers error that suggests the worker itself is throwing an unhandled exception - maybe the request format is off or there's a deeper issue with how the endpoint is configured.","thinkingSignature":"4676ebd78b84b8b2a48d3bac523c3ae546eb4b7ff4e37d9e2980a664c417a257"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_9y1n0q49cojn_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with minimal content to test if POST even works\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat test\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":7552,"output":461,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21695,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780471982270,"responseId":"066f0bae4a4d0a93d9203d69025ccff9"}}
