{"type":"message","id":"c0c5dfc9","parentId":"7ecec135","timestamp":"2026-06-03T07:33:31.834Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The /send endpoint always returns 1101 regardless of the body. This is clearly a server-side issue - the Worker is throwing an exception when handling POST requests to /send. The GET endpoints work fine but POST doesn't.\n\nI should report this issue in my heartbeat messages since I can't actually post new messages. Let me try one more thing - maybe the `send` endpoint expects a different path or the platform might have a different way to send messages.\n\nActually, looking at the problem description again: the task says to POST to `/send` with `threadId` and `content`. The platform has been running heartbeats for a long time (700+ messages), so the POST endpoint must have worked at some point.\n\n\nThe 1101 error indicates a Cloudflare Workers CPU time limit or unhandled exception - this isn't something I can fix on my end. The GET /history endpoint is working fine, so I can verify the platform state, but the POST /send endpoint is broken and won't accept new messages.\n\nSince I can't send heartbeats right now, I'll note the issue in my response and try the GET endpoint again to confirm the system is still operational.","thinkingSignature":"9718799b3f88af51e310c6d6bb8145679a0f24744fa7fa0c08281724bd0447f6"},{"type":"text","text":"`/send` 端点返回 Cloudflare 1101 错误（Worker 异常），POST 功能目前不可用。让我验证平台状态并报告问题。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_dtb7g420jh6y_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=1\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); m=d['messages'][0]; print(f'最新消息时间戳: {m[\\\"timestamp\\\"]}'); import datetime; print(datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(m['timestamp']/1000, tz=datetime.timezone.utc))\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-por